  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Disclaimer",
      "text": "**!important:** In most cases, you should not use `Input` in your application.\n`Input` is a base for other inputs and was not designed to be used directly.\nUse `Input` to create custom inputs, for other cases prefer [TextInput](/core/text-input/)\nor other component.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "text": "`Input` component is used as base for some other inputs ([NativeSelect](/core/native-select/), [TextInput](/core/text-input/), [Textarea](/core/textarea/), etc.).\nThe purpose of the `Input` is to provide shared styles and features to other inputs.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Change input element",
      "text": "Input is a [polymorphic component](/guides/polymorphic), the default root element is `input`,\nbut it can be changed to any other element or component.\n\nExample of using `Input` as `button` and `select`:\n\nExample of using [react-imask](https://github.com/uNmAnNeR/imaskjs/tree/master/packages/react-imask) with `Input`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Input.Wrapper component",
      "text": "`Input.Wrapper` component is used in all other inputs\n([TextInput](/core/text-input/), [NativeSelect](/core/native-select/), [Textarea](/core/textarea/), etc.)\nunder the hood, you _do not need to wrap your inputs with it, as it is already included in all of them_.\nUse `Input.Wrapper` only when you want to create custom inputs.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "inputWrapperOrder",
      "text": "`inputWrapperOrder` allows configuring the order of `Input.Wrapper` parts.\nIt accepts an array of four elements: `label`, `input`, `error` and `description`.\nNote that it is not required to include all of them, you can use only those that you need\n– parts that are not included will not be rendered.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "inputContainer",
      "text": "With `inputContainer` prop, you can enhance inputs that use `Input.Wrapper` under the hood,\nfor example, you can add [Tooltip](/core/tooltip/) to the [TextInput](/core/text-input/) when\nthe input is focused:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "required and withAsterisk props",
      "text": "All components that are based on `Input.Wrapper` support `required` and `withAsterisk` props.\nWhen set to true, both of these props will add a red asterisk to the end of the label.\nThe only difference is whether input element will have `required` attribute, example with\n[TextInput](/core/text-input/) component:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "error prop",
      "text": "All inputs that use `Input.Wrapper` under the hood support `error` prop.\nWhen set to `true`, it will add a red border to the input. You can also pass a React node to display\nan error message below the input. To only display error message without a red border, set `error` prop\nto React node and `withErrorStyles={false}`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Input.Label, Input.Description and Input.Error components",
      "text": "`Input.Label`, `Input.Error` and `Input.Description` components can be used to create custom\nform layouts if the default `Input.Wrapper` layout does not meet your requirements.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Input.Placeholder component",
      "text": "`Input.Placeholder` component can be used to add placeholder to `Input` and `InputBase` components that are based on `button` element\nor do not support placeholder property natively:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Input.ClearButton component",
      "text": "Use `Input.ClearButton` component to add clear button to custom inputs\nbased on `Input` component. `size` of the clear button is automatically\ninherited from the input:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Default props on theme",
      "text": "You can add [default props](/theming/default-props/) on [theme](/theming/theme-object/)\nto `Input` and `Input.Wrapper` components. These default props will be inherited by all inputs\nthat use `Input` and `Input.Wrapper` under the hood ([TextInput](/core/text-input/), [NativeSelect](/core/native-select/), [Textarea](/core/textarea/), etc.):",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Styles on theme",
      "text": "Same as with default props, you can use `Input` and `Input.Wrapper` [Styles API](/styles/styles-api/)\non [theme](/theming/theme-object/) to add styles to all inputs:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Change focus styles",
      "text": "Use `&:focus-within` selector to change inputs focus styles. You can apply these styles to\none component with `classNames` prop or to all inputs with [Styles API](/styles/styles-api/)\non [theme](/theming/theme-object/).",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "InputBase component",
      "text": "`InputBase` component combines `Input` and `Input.Wrapper` components and supports `component` prop:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Styles API",
      "text": "`Input` and `Input.Wrapper` components support [Styles API](/styles/styles-api) –\nyou can customize styles of any inner element with `classNames` and `styles` props.\n\n`Input` Styles API selectors:\n\n`Input.Wrapper` Styles API selectors:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "text": "If you use `Input` component without associated label element, set `aria-label`:\n\nWhen you use `Input` with `Input.Wrapper` it is required to set `id` on both components\nto connect label and other elements with the input:\n\nYou can use [use-id](/hooks/use-id) to generate unique ids:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
